        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "1cd30e46-861f-50b1-b439-adbfe9dcd79f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Eddie Vedder, Matt Cameron, Mike McCready, Stone Gossard, Brendan O'Brien\n- Organizations: Pearl Jam\n- Products: \"The Fixer\", \"Backspacer\", \"Ten\", \"Yield\"\n- Roles: vocalist, drummer, guitarist, producer\n- Topics: songwriting, recording, single release\n\nFacts:\n- Brendan O'Brien had worked on every Pearl Jam album except the 1991 debut \"Ten\" and the 2006 self-titled record, but \"Backspacer\" was his first production credit for the band since \"Yield\" in 1998.\n- Pearl Jam recorded \"Backspacer\" from February through April 2009 with producer Brendan O'Brien.\n- Eddie Vedder wrote the lyrics for \"The Fixer,\" and Matt Cameron, Mike McCready, and Stone Gossard co-wrote its music.\n- Pearl Jam released \"The Fixer\" on August 24, 2009 as the first single from their ninth studio album, \"Backspacer\" (2009).",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
